From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wineboot: PS5: a prefix without DefaultInstall's last service is updated again.

A tester's Alpha 4 Steam (2026-10-29, fw 12.20) never showed its sign-in: steam.exe
asserted "GetAdaptersAddresses returned 2", the webhelper's browser retried \\.\Nsi
144 times and its renderer never loaded Steam's page, so after 30 s Steam's
transport gave up ("Failed to reconnect to websocket"), shut down and relaunched,
twice. The prefix's services.exe loaded four services (MountMgr, the Steam Client
Service, winebth, wineusb) where a working prefix loads about twenty: PreInstall
had run, DefaultInstall had not, so there was no nsiproxy service and no \\.\Nsi.

wineboot cannot tell: a rundll32 that does not start returns no handle and the
loop goes on, and one that ends early is waited for like one that finished. Patch
0952 writes .update-timestamp after the update, so such a prefix is marked current
and wine.inf's content-derived time keeps it so across builds.

DefaultInstall registers nsiproxy last in each [DefaultInstall.*.Services]
section (checked by tests/test_wineboot_install_sentinel.py). A prefix without it
is updated at every start, and the timestamp is written only once it has it.
A complete prefix is not affected; a broken one is repaired by its next start
(about 75 s of update, during which AddService's start flag starts nsiproxy).
---
 programs/wineboot/wineboot.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
--- a/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
+++ b/programs/wineboot/wineboot.c
@@ -1731,6 +1731,20 @@
     CertCloseStore( store, 0 );
 }
 
+/* PS5: wine.inf's DefaultInstall registers nsiproxy last ([DefaultInstall.*.Services]), so a prefix without it never
+ * finished DefaultInstall: a first session cut short, or a rundll32 that did not start or ended early, both of which
+ * wineboot does not see. Such a prefix has no \\.\Nsi, GetAdaptersAddresses fails with error 2 and the game store's
+ * client never shows its sign-in (a tester's Alpha 4 prefix, 2026-10-29). It is updated until it has it. */
+static BOOL ps5_default_install_done(void)
+{
+    HKEY key;
+
+    if (RegOpenKeyExW( HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE, L"System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\nsiproxy", 0, KEY_QUERY_VALUE, &key ))
+        return FALSE;
+    RegCloseKey( key );
+    return TRUE;
+}
+
 /* execute rundll32 on the wine.inf file if necessary */
 static void update_wineprefix( BOOL force )
 {
@@ -1753,7 +1767,7 @@
     fstat( fd, &st );
     close( fd );
 
-    if (update_timestamp( config_dir, st.st_mtime, TRUE ) || force)
+    if (update_timestamp( config_dir, st.st_mtime, TRUE ) || force || !ps5_default_install_done())
     {
         HANDLE process;
         DWORD count = 0;
@@ -1785,7 +1799,9 @@
         update_user_profile();
         update_win_version();
         update_root_certs();
-        update_timestamp( config_dir, st.st_mtime, FALSE );
+        if (ps5_default_install_done()) update_timestamp( config_dir, st.st_mtime, FALSE );
+        else ERR( "wine.inf's DefaultInstall did not finish in %s; the next start updates it again\n",
+                  debugstr_w(prettyprint_configdir()) );
 
         TRACE( "wine: configuration in %s has been updated.\n", debugstr_w(prettyprint_configdir()) );
     }
-- 
